.TH UPC\-TTY\-BRIDGE 1 "2026-10-29" "unheaded b06c570c" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
upc\-tty\-bridge \- Bridge UPC TTY byte streams to browser terminals over WebSocket (ASCEND\-LINUX Mode A).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B upc\-tty\-bridge
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bridge UPC TTY byte streams to browser terminals over WebSocket (ASCEND\-LINUX Mode A).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-listen \fISTRING\fR
listen address (host:port); loopback by default (default 127.0.0.1:26100)
.TP
.B \-\-port \fIN\fR
deprecated: listen on 127.0.0.1:<port> (use \-\-listen)
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
upc\-tty\-bridge \-\-port 26100
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
